      "classification": "semantically_covered_with_preserved_unix_hardening",
      "decisions": [
        "ScopeLaneFileWalV1::open already requests write(true) on Windows and append(true) on other systems, read/create/truncate(false), holds LockedFile ownership, and explicitly seeks to end for append. Current additional Unix O_NOFOLLOW, mode 0600 and inode checks must remain.",
        "The complete torn-tail recovery regression is present: commit first frame, fsync partial tail, recover/truncate exactly to prior length, append sequence 2, reopen and verify both envelopes. Current checked Option access avoids expect/index panic without reducing the assertions.",
        "Historical Windows WAL workflow remains with all original crash-recovery execution and checkout identity checks. Current workflow additionally watches crate manifests/lib/toolchain, enables long checkout paths and uses a newer pinned toolchain action. Retain those improvements."
      ],
